      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.1,
          "end": 4.8,
          "en": "Now that we've finished this app here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.8,
          "end": 6.96,
          "en": "and now that we've finished",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.96,
          "end": 9,
          "en": "this course section here in general",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9,
          "end": 12.87,
          "en": "and we learned about many crucial flutter and Dart features,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.87,
          "end": 14.85,
          "en": "I wanna end this section",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.85,
          "end": 18.6,
          "en": "by diving into three Dart features you should know,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.6,
          "end": 20.85,
          "en": "which are totally optional though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.85,
          "end": 24.42,
          "en": "which you don't have to use in this or other projects,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.42,
          "end": 26.04,
          "en": "but what you might want to use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.04,
          "end": 29.67,
          "en": "or what you might see in other projects you are working on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.67,
          "end": 32.55,
          "en": "And also features we will use from time to time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.55,
          "end": 34.14,
          "en": "throughout the rest of this course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 34.14,
          "end": 36.78,
          "en": "which is why you should know about them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 36.78,
          "end": 39.93,
          "en": "And I wanna start here in the quiz Dart file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 39.93,
          "end": 43.11,
          "en": "There we have this QuizState class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 43.11,
          "end": 46.02,
          "en": "which is this state class for the quiz widget.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 46.02,
          "end": 48.39,
          "en": "And you learned that stateful widgets",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 48.39,
          "end": 51.48,
          "en": "are basically split across these two classes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 51.48,
          "end": 53.55,
          "en": "Now the QuizState class here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 53.55,
          "end": 57.54,
          "en": "is actually called underscore QuizState.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 57.54,
          "end": 60.81,
          "en": "And I mentioned earlier in this section",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 60.81,
          "end": 62.04,
          "en": "that this leading underscore",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 62.04,
          "end": 66.09,
          "en": "is a Dart-specific thing in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 66.09,
          "end": 69.63,
          "en": "By adding an underscore in front of a class name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 69.63,
          "end": 74.03999999999999,
          "en": "you tell Dart that this class is meant to be private",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 74.03999999999999,
          "end": 78.66,
          "en": "and should basically only be usable inside of this file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 78.66,
          "end": 81.06,
          "en": "But if another file would import quiz.Dart,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 81.06,
          "end": 84.663,
          "en": "it would not be able to access this QuizState class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 86.1,
          "end": 88.77,
          "en": "The reason for that is that this QuizState class",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 88.77,
          "end": 90.84,
          "en": "really belongs to this quiz class",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 90.84,
          "end": 92.78999999999999,
          "en": "and should therefore not be used outside",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 92.78999999999999,
          "end": 95.37,
          "en": "of this file in any other context.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 95.37,
          "end": 98.22,
          "en": "The quiz class then also does not have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 98.22,
          "end": 102,
          "en": "that leading underscore because it indeed is not private,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 102,
          "end": 104.22,
          "en": "but publicly available.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 104.22,
          "end": 106.47,
          "en": "Now that is not a new concept of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 106.47,
          "end": 107.75999999999999,
          "en": "I mentioned it before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 107.75999999999999,
          "end": 110.07,
          "en": "but it is a concept you should keep in mind.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 110.07,
          "end": 112.11,
          "en": "But what you should know is that you cannot",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 112.11,
          "end": 114.69,
          "en": "just turn classes into private classes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 114.69,
          "end": 117.63,
          "en": "by adding such a underscore, but all the properties",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 117.63,
          "end": 120.39,
          "en": "and methods inside of classes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 120.39,
          "end": 121.32,
          "en": "We could, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 121.32,
          "end": 124.62,
          "en": "convert selected answers to a private property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 124.62,
          "end": 126.483,
          "en": "by adding a leading underscore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 127.35,
          "end": 129.87,
          "en": "Of course, we have to do that in all the places",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 129.87,
          "end": 132.9,
          "en": "where selected answers is used thereafter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 132.9,
          "end": 134.46,
          "en": "Otherwise we have an error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 134.46,
          "end": 136.683,
          "en": "that some identifier can't be found.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 138.09,
          "end": 139.82999999999998,
          "en": "But with that, you would make it clear",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 139.82999999999998,
          "end": 142.05,
          "en": "that selected answers is really meant",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 142.05,
          "end": 145.62,
          "en": "to be only used inside of this file here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 145.62,
          "end": 149.49,
          "en": "And if another file could get access to the QuizState class",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 149.49,
          "end": 151.92000000000002,
          "en": "because it maybe would not be private,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 151.92000000000002,
          "end": 154.77,
          "en": "then that other code in another file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 154.77,
          "end": 158.19,
          "en": "should still not be able to access selected answers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 158.19,
          "end": 160.41,
          "en": "because even though the class is now public,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 160.41,
          "end": 163.41,
          "en": "this is still marked as a private property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 163.41,
          "end": 165.03,
          "en": "that should only be usable inside",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 165.03,
          "end": 166.833,
          "en": "of this file here essentially.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 168.21,
          "end": 171.03,
          "en": "Now here, I'll switch this back to a private class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 171.03,
          "end": 173.43,
          "en": "and this is not something you have to do here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 173.43,
          "end": 175.98,
          "en": "It's not important for this app we're building here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 175.98,
          "end": 178.5,
          "en": "but you will sometimes see property names",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 178.5,
          "end": 180.75,
          "en": "that start with leading underscores.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 180.75,
          "end": 183.42,
          "en": "And it is important to understand that this in the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 183.42,
          "end": 187.77,
          "en": "means that these are private properties or private methods,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 187.77,
          "end": 189.99,
          "en": "you can add such an underscore there as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 189.99,
          "end": 192.33,
          "en": "And this simply means that those properties",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 192.33,
          "end": 195.84,
          "en": "and methods are meant to be only used inside of the file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 195.84,
          "end": 197.94,
          "en": "where the class is defined.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 197.94,
          "end": 200.76,
          "en": "And if the class is the only thing defined in a file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 200.76,
          "end": 202.68,
          "en": "then those properties and methods",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 202.68,
          "end": 205.5,
          "en": "would essentially be private to that class",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 205.5,
          "end": 208.35,
          "en": "and would not be usable anywhere else in your code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 208.35,
          "end": 209.823,
          "en": "in any other file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 210.66,
          "end": 212.94299999999998,
          "en": "So that's what this syntax is all about.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 214.47,
          "end": 216.9,
          "en": "Another Dart feature, which is optional,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 216.9,
          "end": 219.81,
          "en": "but which you should know about are gatherers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 219.81,
          "end": 221.61,
          "en": "And I can show you a great example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 221.61,
          "end": 225.63,
          "en": "for a gather here in the results screen widget class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 225.63,
          "end": 228.6,
          "en": "There we have this get summary data method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 228.6,
          "end": 231.09,
          "en": "which in the end simply produces a list",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 231.09,
          "end": 232.383,
          "en": "which it then returns.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 233.22,
          "end": 235.35,
          "en": "And this list which it produces",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 235.35,
          "end": 239.16,
          "en": "is based on this chosen answer's property in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 239.16,
          "end": 241.32,
          "en": "that and this questions list,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 241.32,
          "end": 243.9,
          "en": "which we defined in another file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 243.9,
          "end": 247.59,
          "en": "Now defining this as a method like this is absolutely fine,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 247.59,
          "end": 249.63,
          "en": "but if you have methods like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 249.63,
          "end": 253.53,
          "en": "which take no input values, no parameters,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 253.53,
          "end": 256.5,
          "en": "and which in the end then just produce some data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 256.5,
          "end": 258.99,
          "en": "based on some other class properties,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 258.99,
          "end": 261.03,
          "en": "you could also use a gather instead,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 261.03,
          "end": 263.613,
          "en": "by using an alternative Dart syntax.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 264.57,
          "end": 268.02,
          "en": "For that syntax you would rename that method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 268.02,
          "end": 270.27,
          "en": "to sound more like a property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 270.27,
          "end": 273.33,
          "en": "so that it would describe data that's inside of it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 273.33,
          "end": 274.92,
          "en": "For example, summaryData.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 274.92,
          "end": 276.853,
          "en": "Instead of get summaryData.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 277.71,
          "end": 279.93,
          "en": "You would then remove those parentheses",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 279.93,
          "end": 283.38,
          "en": "and instead add the get keyword in front of it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 283.38,
          "end": 287.55,
          "en": "This is a special keyword in Dart, which creates a getter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 287.55,
          "end": 290.90999999999997,
          "en": "And a getter in the end is still a method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 290.90999999999997,
          "end": 293.46,
          "en": "You still have your function body here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 293.46,
          "end": 295.40999999999997,
          "en": "this code still executes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 295.40999999999997,
          "end": 299.34000000000003,
          "en": "but you don't call summaryData like a method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 299.34000000000003,
          "end": 302.34,
          "en": "So you don't call summaryData like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 302.34,
          "end": 304.17,
          "en": "with parentheses thereafter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 304.17,
          "end": 308.49,
          "en": "but instead you simply refer to it as a variable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 308.49,
          "end": 311.1,
          "en": "So now here we would have some name duplication",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 311.1,
          "end": 313.74,
          "en": "and creating this extra final variable here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 313.74,
          "end": 315.78,
          "en": "would now simply be redundant.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 315.78,
          "end": 317.88,
          "en": "Instead, I can get rid of that line here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 317.88,
          "end": 321.66,
          "en": "and I can now still access summary data like a property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 321.66,
          "end": 324.9,
          "en": "or like a variable that does not change,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 324.9,
          "end": 327.51,
          "en": "even though under the hood it's a method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 327.51,
          "end": 329.67,
          "en": "But because of this get keyword,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 329.67,
          "end": 333.03,
          "en": "this in the end can be used like a property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 333.03,
          "end": 335.4,
          "en": "by accessing it like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 335.4,
          "end": 337.92,
          "en": "but internally it behaves like a method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 337.92,
          "end": 340.17,
          "en": "So that's another Dart feature which you can use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 340.17,
          "end": 342.96,
          "en": "as an alternative to defining a method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 342.96,
          "end": 345.39,
          "en": "And it's great for use cases like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 345.39,
          "end": 349.47,
          "en": "where you have a method that in the end just transforms data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 349.47,
          "end": 353.22,
          "en": "that's stored in another property of the class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 353.22,
          "end": 356.22,
          "en": "Another example for a method that could be converted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 356.22,
          "end": 360.51,
          "en": "to a gather can be found in the quiz-question Dart file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 360.51,
          "end": 363.33,
          "en": "There we have this getShuffledAnswers method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 363.33,
          "end": 366.18,
          "en": "which in the end also is just such a gather.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 366.18,
          "end": 369.51,
          "en": "It takes another class property, answers,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 369.51,
          "end": 373.35,
          "en": "and then derives some data based on that property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 373.35,
          "end": 376.56,
          "en": "So here we could also rename this to shuffledAnswers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 376.56,
          "end": 380.25,
